  "summary": "The paper proposes a single‑qudit variational quantum neural network for credit‑risk prediction on the 30,000‑sample Taiwan credit dataset. The QNN achieves macro‑F1 ≈0.667±0.015 with 384 parameters—outperforming logistic regression (0.601) and approaching random forest (0.647) and classical neural networks (0.682)—while producing feature‑importance rankings with edit distance ≈20.9 to LR and maintaining F1 ≈0.632 under feature‑poisoning noise.",
